he Prophetﷺ, when he gets better.", "OK, no problem We can bring a piece of paper. No problem But right now he's ill and sick, so let's move away. Let's not do that. Let's not bother the Prophetﷺ That's all 'Umar is saying But they will turn this thing into: Oh! He's disobeying the Prophet, and all of this stuff So! 'Umar Ibn alKhattab here, out of care for the Prophetﷺ, he says that we have the book of Allah We have it, and it's sufficient for us And I'm going to go on into what 'Umar means by that But he's not only 'Umar saying that, because in the same narration, you see that people disagreed So there was a group of people who were of the same opinion of 'Umar Ibn AlKhattab, and there was another group of people who were against that So, because they disagreed and their voices were loud, etc.", "they disturbed the Prophetﷺ who was already ill So He said, leave me or go away He didn't say \"Get out of my home\", like \"kicked out of the house\" as he tries to push. No! He just said, leave me because he's sick, he's ill and they're fighting Prophetﷺ told them to bring this piece of paper, But they are fighting and disagreeing with each other instead of doing that So the Prophetﷺ told them to leave – leave him. That's it! That's what the narration is saying",))
