 \"Yeah, we know we know the devastating war. We've like we've been through that. What's What's this humiliation? What's this humiliating peace that you speak of?\" So, he said, \"Um we take away your weapons and your armor, and whatever we had taken from you in war, we keep to ourselves, and whatever you took away from us at war, you have to return to us, and you pay the blood money for those of us that you have killed.", "And those of you that were killed are in hellfire. And you allow your people to just chase the camels until Allah and the caliph of the messenger and the Muhajirin decide to excuse you. Okay? Now, uh Abu Bakr basically presented this to the people as his desire, as his will, and out of all the people there, one person said that he disagreed with a part of it. And that person was Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. He said, \"Um that he himself uh a different view. And he would like to present it.", "So, he says that to that what you what you've mentioned from a devastating war and a humiliating peace, then yes, you know, that's definitely you know, a good idea. And that which you've said about um we keeping what we took from you in war and you returning what you took from us, um referring to Banu Assad and Ghatafan, then yes, you know, that's a great idea as well um and Omar is upon that. As for the last clause, okay? That they pay the blood money and that their dead are in hellfire, then those that died from our people, those that were killed, the Muslims that were killed, they were killed due to them following the orders and commands of Allah.", "And their compensation will be from Allah. We do not accept blood money. And then the people agreed with what Omar said. And that was what occurred and that is how the peace was made. The compensations wouldn't be small. Compensations sometimes would range from 10 camels per person that was killed to 50. Um if it was someone of a mass of rank, it could go up to 100, 200, 1,000. So, such a thing would be one debilitating to the tribe that has to pay the blood money. Um and it would be a massive boost to the finances of those who've had relatives that were killed or who have had uh troops and companions that were killed.", "But Omar refused. Omar was sincere. Omar was someone that was certain that the compensation would be from Allah Subhana Wa Ta'ala. It doesn't need to be from the disbelievers that went to war with the Muslims. And that in itself is a beautiful sign of the sincerity of Omar and those that agreed with him. And of course, that's how the whole matter ended and the people accepted what Omar had to say and what he offered. Even things like the sincerity of the prophet, peace be upon him, is definitely a proof of prophethood. Okay? Because Okay, you have all these reports about him doing these amazing things, but proving that he's sincere in his call adds, of course, to the claim of his prophethood.", "Similarly here, when you find his companions, the ones closest to him in proximity, through blood ties, when they are showing signs of complete sincerity, you come to the conclusion that Oh, okay. So, clearly the people that were closest to him, that were most aware of of his situation, truly believed in his message. And just to drive the point further, here's an additional report that I'd just like to mention very briefly, just a part of it in the famous reports about Omar ibn al-Khattab and how he was killed. The report actually mentions that when he used to pray, the first rak'ah, he used to sometimes read Surat Yusuf or Surat an-Nahl.", "All right? Now, that in itself says something. But by the way, guys, Surat Yusuf Surat an-Nahl is like verses. How common is that? For the Shi'as that are watching this video, when you think about Omar, you're assuming that he's someone who is completely insincere. Why wouldn't he just recite Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad instead? Why would he recite something as lengthy as Surah Yusuf or Surah An-Nahl? It's because of his attachment to the Quran. It's because he was someone that enjoyed it. And there's so many reports about the sincerity of Omar. However, you know, it's not like um they're all gathered in one place.", "You just read narrations, and you just come across them randomly like the way I did with the first report. Anyways, guys, yes, I do mainly do refutations on this channel. However, if you'd like to see more of this sort of content, then do let me know in the comments below. And if you'd like to actually support the channel, then please feel free to pick up the Sirah map one that includes all the major locations in the Sirah. You can find the link to it in the pinned comment below. I'll catch you guys in the next one. Assalamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuh.",))
