#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Ok! This seems interesting, let's have a look! That means you have تعصُّب (Fanaticism) for it. That means that you don't take anything else, this is the only.. This is the way, this is everything. Which a lot of people do, especially in certain parts from the Indian subcontinent etc.. So, he's saying that this is not permissible. Let's continue listening to it and maybe, that will upset some people, but let's listen to what the Sheikh is saying, and then we'll explain and expound upon what he says as well, because I'm sure there's a lot more context to it He says that he would say: \"I would only follow the Madhab (School of Thought), I do not go anywhere else, and not take anything else, only the Madhab of Imam Ahmad\" or only the Madhab Shafi’i, etc.", "He's saying that: that's not permissible The only Madhab that you.. He means, in this case, that you do not go against, that you do not oppose, that you follow in every.. You say \"that's the end-all and be-all\", is the teachings of the Prophetﷺ, meaning the Hadith, obviously, and the tradition of the Prophetﷺ This is the only Madhab that you take. This is the Madhab of the Muslims. It's obedience and following the Prophetﷺ This obedience and طاعة or لا متبوع بحقّ إلا محمدٍﷺ (There's one to be worthy of being followed absolutely and completely) is The Prophet Muhammadﷺ.", "No one else! The other remaining scholars, you take from them and you leave, because they make mistakes, They're human beings and that's what Imam Malik said. He said that \"everyone you take from and you reject Except the specific person in this grave\" referring to the Prophetﷺ, and he pointed at the grave of the Prophetﷺ, Now, there's a common argument that people make. The people who just stick to the Madhab and the Madhab is everything, They will say to you, \"But didn't Shafi'i follow the Prophetﷺ? Didn’t Imam Ahmad follow the Prophetﷺ? Wasn't their Madhab following the Prophetﷺ?\".", "Yes! but that doesn't mean that every single person what they said is right, And the evidence for that is that, they disagreed with one another, that Imam Ahmed disagreed with Shafi'i, And Shafi'i disagreed with Malik and they disagreed with one another, which shows that, If they're all –as you try to claim– sourcing the Hadith, that means they will not disagree with each other If they disagree with each other, that means that some of them can be correct and some of them can be wrong, That means you cannot 100% take every single thing they say as if it is Revelation.", "You cannot do that with the Madhab Then he says –It's a very strong point– none of the 4 Imams of the Madhahib have said to you \"Just follow me, follow my Madhab!\" In fact, all of them said, \"If what I say goes against the Hadith or the Quran, then reject it!\". That's what they said, With them saying this, it is evidence by itself that they can make mistakes. And certain positions they can take, can be rejected Yes, this is the point that we're making, and he's adding to it that they were students of each other I was talking about them disagreeing with each other.", "They were the students of one another And you didn't have Imam Ahmad saying: \"I'm a Shafi'i Madhab\". He disagreed with him! Even the companions of Imam Shafi'i like Almuzani المُزني disagreed with him on certain issues And the companions of Abu Hanifah etc. disagreed with him.. So, people need to understand, that even the main students of these Imams, they even disagreed with the Imams And obviously, we're talking about Jurisprudence and Fiqh in these issues, they disagreed with them So, you cannot come and say, \"This is end-all, be-all and, 100%, what is said is the truth\" Here, he is saying that \"it's not permissible to say\" which means that this is probably the question that came, That it's not permissible to force the people \"You have to follow this specific Madhab!\".", "This is probably how the question came, There are certain people who say that, you have to follow this Madhab, you have to follow that Madhab. This is probably the context of the video You cannot force people by saying that, you have to stick to this Madhab The only Madhab you have to stick to is the Madhab of Prophet Muhammadﷺ and the Quran This is the only Madhab that YOU HAVE TO, you have no choice except following Now, but what about following a Madhab as a guideline? Because this Madhabs gives guidelines They give rulings, they give أصول (Principles) which guide you as a student of knowledge There's no problem in doing that.", "Also, don't think that the Sheikh is saying that you cannot follow a Madhab, What he's saying is that; you cannot force people to take a Madhab which many people do sadly He's saying you cannot say that you have to be upon a specific Madhab to another individual. You cannot do that But if you yourself want to follow a Madhab, there's no issue with that as long as –as this video says– You cannot be 100% whatever the Madhab says is Revelation, because there are things in your Madhab –whatever Madhab you would follow– that would be incorrect, that would be in opposition to the Majority, That would be in opposition to the Hadith, that would be in opposition to the Text So, if you find that, then you go against the Madhab that you're following in that specific issue But using the Madhab to give you specific guidelines and foundations, so they can help you as a student of knowledge", "to evolve and learn, there's no issue in doing that, and even the Sheikh, I'm sure many videos of his will say that What he's saying there is slightly different, but I hope people understand the idea",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"Clip-React| No Bible Contradictions? Following Mazhab? Mahdi Is Dajjal and more.. | Muhammed Ali\"")
