// T ML236 1172,1173,1174,1175,1176,1177,1178,1179,1180,1181,1182,1183,1184,1185,1186,1187,1188,1189,1190,1191,1192,1193,1194,1195,1196,1197,1198,1199,1200,1201,1202,1203,1204,1205,1206,1207,1208,1209,1210,1211,1212,1213,1214,1215,1216,1217,1218,1219,1220,1221,1222,1223,1224,1225,1226,1227,1228,1229,1230,1231,1232 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Four, no. Madhahib were many, many, more. The ones that reach us today that we're following are four There was the Madhab of Awza'i, the Madhab of alHassan alBasri There was many, many Madhahib The Madhab of Sufyan atThawri These were Madhahib, but the students, they were not collecting or writing it, the students of these السلف الصالح (The righteous predecessors) they were not writing and collecting and establishing the same way Madhab adhDhahiri is very well known, Ibn Hazm, if you hear about him, he's a follower of Madhab adhDhahiri, by Abu Dawood adhDhahiri - it's another Madhab These are Madhab But the ones that are established and have reached us are 4 Because their students, they collected and wrote it and spread it around And these 4 are the ones we know The Shafi'i, the Hanbali, the Maliki, and the Hanafi - These 4 The only reason is because their students expounded upon them.", "Now, do these Madhahib agree with each other in everything? And if the answer is no, then someone has to be wrong and someone has to be right We're not talking about reward now Because they're all reward for their أجتهاد (ijtihad: independent juristic reasoning) If they did correct, independent reasoning, trying to find the evidences, and they made a mistake, Allah rewards them for trying If they did and said the truth, they get two rewards One for trying and one for finding the truth or saying the truth or teaching the truth But if they disagree, then when it comes to Quran and Sunnah, there is one correct and one incorrect And if this is the case, then that which establishes the truth is the evidences from the Quran and the Sunnah That which establishes the truth is the evidence from the Quran and the Sunnah But what about following a Madhab?", "You can follow a Madhab And the reason you can, especially if you're going to become a student of knowledge, is it gives you structure It makes things easier, learning and studying easier for you It gives you principles, gives you books of explanation, of a Ahadith It gives you, where you can go, where you cannot go - it gives you structure, it helps you learning But most of the people that when they become علماء (scholars), they study one Madhab and then the other Madhab and then the other And then they become a مجتهد (Mujtahid: doing ijtihad) in the Madhab That's how it happens But you start somewhere, you start with a Madhab, it gives you structure, it helps you learning There is no issues with learning and studying a Madhab There's no issues with that, no problems But the problem is when your Madhab has a view which is incorrect, that the majority reject,", "and there's clear evidences, but you still say, I'm following the Madhab Brother, what do you do? The Madhab is the Madhab, it's my Madhab No, brother! in this case, in which is NOT a valid disagreement, in which there are strong evidences for both sides, and it's an issue which is very difficult We have Companions here, Companions there, evidences here and evidences there, which is OK, you can take different positions But when it is something that has no strong evidences, very weak evidences, and the opposite has very clear teachings from the Prophetﷺ, you cannot say, I'm following my Madhab!", "There's no تعصب (Ta'assub: fanaticism) means just blind, 100% following of anyone, except the Messengerﷺ So this is it If someone wants to become a student of knowledge and follow a Madhab, you're welcome to do so Understanding then this and bearing it in mind, when there is overwhelming evidence against the Madhab that you're in, you take that But you stick with the other things and the principles of your Madhab, OK?",))
#source("Source: The Muslim Lantern, \"Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali\"")
