#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Yes, there are many. Actually, Abu Hanifa himself -may Allah have mercy on him- he said -Not only him but all of the Imams of the 4 schools of thought in Islam- they said that if anything I say goes against the text, reject it And whenever they saw evidence of opposing some of what they believed in, they changed it A prominent example of that is Imam Ashafi'i, who was another imam of another School of Though, the Shafi'i School of Thought He had one position when he was in one land and when he traveled in Iraq and Egypt He changed many of his views when he came across a lot of the evidence that he did not know before So he changed his previous positions to new positions And this is the easy way for us, the work is all done.", "What we need to do as Muslims is we look at the scholarly opinions. We look at the evidence If there is evidence supporting, and most of the time, the overwhelming majority of the scholars will have the evidence And the people who didn't, they probably have missed the evidence here or there, which is very easily demonstrated Because they don't have evidence to support their point. So we will go with the overwhelming majority of the scholars And the Guidance is already there and present in every civilisation. And if you read these books and research, you'll find it",))
