#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Yes And I'm going to answer this, then I'm going to ask you a few questions Because I've given you plenty of time to ask me questions and there are people in the backstage as well. So, the reason is very simple The reason is not everyone defers to the evidence when there's a disagreement There are people who have diseases in their hearts. There are people who like to follow their own desires There are people who intentionally want to change the text There are people with harmful intentions. There are hypocrites that pretend to be Muslims while they're not Muslims There are many reasons why you will have certain people disagreeing and changing the teachings of Islam because they just don't like what the text says And that does not change the reality that the Guidance is there.", "And if you were to look, you would find the Guidance in the end And that the Quran itself teaches you, If you disagree over anything, you have to return it to the text It's mentioned explicitly in the Quran chapter 4 (Annissa4:59) That: (Obey Allah, obey the Messenger and those in authority among you.. And if you disagree over anything, if you defer over anything, return it to Allah and the Messenger) So Allah tells us what to do. And not everyone follows the instructions given in the Quran",))
